2026-10-22T07:05:00Z  CLAIM    T0206 normal exit skipped Application::quit(), so last_session.m3u and CONFIG.save never ran on window close or Qt.quit()
2026-10-22T07:05:00Z  CHANGE   src/core/Application.hpp: aboutToQuit is a slot, not a signal nobody connected to; it is wired to QGuiApplication::aboutToQuit at Application.cpp:577 and owns the whole teardown (both recording halves, the session playlist, audio stop, CONFIG.save when dirty).
2026-10-22T07:05:00Z  CHANGE   src/core/Application.cpp: quit() only calls qapp_->quit(). Calling the teardown there too is what made the SIGINT path run it twice and the window-close path run it zero times.
2026-10-22T07:05:00Z  BLOCKER  A first attempt at this evidence could not run at all: cmake/TargetSetup.cmake decided "did the user name CHADVIS_DEPLOY_BUNDLE?" from cache presence, and option() writes that cache entry on the first configure -- so the fast-profile suppression was dead from the second configure onward, every relink paid the 5-7 minute deploy, and an aborted deploy left a half-deployed bundle that loaded a second Qt (qFatal in the cocoa plugin). Fixed under the same commit: CHADVIS_FORCE_DEPLOY is its own flag, and a suppressed build leaves the bundle bare (no Frameworks, no PlugIns, no qt.conf) instead of inheriting a stale deployed one.
